+# Daily Grind coffee finder
+
+The homepage offers a client-side recommendation from its three featured coffees.
+It does not create orders, send requests, or store personal data. Menu links use
+the homepage's existing routes.
+
+## Browser agent tool
+
+The HTML form declares the WebMCP tool `find_coffee` with `toolname`,
+`tooldescription`, and `toolautosubmit`. Named, labeled selects define its required
+parameters, including `toolparamdescription` annotations:
+
+```json
+{"temperature":"iced","flavor":"smooth"}
+```
+
+- `temperature`: `any`, `hot`, or `iced`
+- `flavor`: `any`, `sweet`, `bold`, or `smooth`
+
+Submitting returns `status`, `preferences`, `exactMatch`, `coffee` (including its
+menu URL), and `message` through `SubmitEvent.respondWith()` for agent invocations.
+Invalid input returns an error status and message. Temperature is a hard filter;
+unavailable flavor combinations receive an explicitly labeled closest match.
+Ties use the order of the featured menu. Each submission replaces the previous
+result in the visible, accessible status region.
+
+Automatic tool discovery requires a browser/agent with declarative WebMCP support.
+The ordinary form works with JavaScript in other browsers. No server or API key
+is needed. See the [declarative WebMCP API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api).
