@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static Vite homepage with an interactive browser-encryption preview.
+
+- `pnpm install`
+- `pnpm build` builds static assets into `dist/`.
+- `pnpm test` runs cryptographic round-trip and tamper-rejection checks without a browser or server.
+
+## Delivery notes
+
+The default suite is the noble `ml_kem768_x25519` hybrid preset. Optional suites use ML-KEM-768 or ephemeral X25519. HKDF-SHA-256 derives a non-extractable AES-256-GCM key. Every save generates fresh recipient keys, encapsulation, a 32-byte salt, and a random 12-byte nonce. A 128-bit GCM authentication tag protects the content and a fixed-order metadata header. The header binds the application, version, suite, recipient fingerprint, encapsulation, salt, nonce, cipher and creation time. Algorithm implementation: https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-post-quantum
+
+This is explicitly a **local preview**, with recipient private keys held in tab memory to demonstrate authenticated decryption. No plaintext or keys are placed in browser storage, transmitted or logged. Saving clears the textarea. Revealed notes hide when the tab loses visibility. Replacing/deleting a note wipes its recipient secret-key byte array on a best-effort basis; JavaScript cannot guarantee complete memory erasure. Refreshing loses the ciphertext and preview recipient keys. Downloaded envelopes contain no private key and cannot be recovered after the preview is cleared.
+
+## Production integration
+
+There is no delivery backend or authenticated store recipient in this repository. Before using for actual delivery: provision recipient public keys through an authenticated, HTTPS channel with key IDs and rotation; keep private keys off the customer client; send only the encrypted envelope to an authenticated delivery API; and decrypt only in the authorized delivery system. Do not reuse the local-preview recipient generation in production. Encryption alone does not authenticate the sender, authorize access, or protect against scripts compromised on the same origin.
+
+The homepage uses remote Unsplash photos and Google Fonts. Delivery-note encryption has no external network dependency once the compiled JavaScript is loaded.
