+# smallpt studio
+
+Kevin Beason’s open-source [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly and rendered in an HTML canvas. Rendering happens entirely on the client in a module Web Worker, with progressive 4-sample passes. No runtime libraries, render service, SharedArrayBuffer, or special isolation headers are required.
+
+The interface includes randomized sphere and wall colors, individual color pickers, palette reset, sample and resolution controls, progress, and PNG export. Changing settings or colors cancels the previous job between row batches. The initial preview was generated using the same adapted C++ renderer; live browser output replaces it after the first complete pass.
+
+## Build
+
+Requires Node.js 20+ and Emscripten (`emcc`) on PATH.
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+npm run check:wasm
+```
+
+`dist/` contains the complete static site. The compiled `public/wasm/smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm` are also checked in, so the source directory is ready for static hosting. Serve over HTTP(S), with `.wasm` served as `application/wasm` for streaming compilation. Emscripten falls back to ArrayBuffer compilation when streaming is unavailable. No server-side rendering is involved.
+
+## Source and license
+
+- `src/smallpt-original.cpp`: unmodified upstream source.
+- `src/smallpt.cpp`: original integrator and scene, with progressive rendering, configurable colors, and an RGBA buffer API replacing the command-line PPM writer. Accumulation remains linear until display conversion.
+- `src/LICENSE.smallpt.txt`: Kevin Beason’s MIT license.
+- `render-worker.js`: buffer transfers, progress, and cancellation.
+- `scripts/build-wasm.sh`: reproducible WebAssembly build flags.
+
+The WebAssembly build reserves a 1 MB stack for smallpt’s recursive light paths. Rendering uses one worker rather than OpenMP. Fonts are requested from Google Fonts with local fallback fonts; all rendering assets are local.
+
+`npm run check:wasm` executes the actual shipped WebAssembly in Node using file-backed fetch responses; it starts no server. Browser verification has intentionally not been performed.
+
+To regenerate the initial 512-sample preview with the same renderer, run `npm run build:preview` (requires `g++` and Python 3), then rebuild the site.
