+# smallpt studio
+
+Kevin Beason’s MIT-licensed smallpt C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. Open `index.html` through any static HTTP host. All interactive rendering runs locally in a dedicated Web Worker; no rendering service or backend is used.
+
+## Build
+
+The compiled `public/smallpt.mjs` and `public/smallpt.wasm` are checked in, so a normal static build needs only Node:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+The output is `dist/`. No dependencies need to be installed. To rebuild the C++ module, install Emscripten and run:
+
+```sh
+npm run build:wasm
+npm test
+```
+
+The Emscripten build reserves a 4 MiB stack for recursive paths, allows linear-memory growth, and needs no SharedArrayBuffer or cross-origin isolation headers.
+
+## Implementation
+
+- `vendor/smallpt.cpp`: original upstream source, unchanged.
+- `vendor/LICENSE.txt`: Kevin Beason’s MIT license.
+- `src/smallpt.cpp`: original scene and radiance integrator with an RGBA framebuffer and progressive C interface replacing the CLI / PPM output loop. Each pass traces one sample per each of four tent-filtered subpixels, adds to persistent floating-point accumulators, and gamma-encodes the average for display. OpenMP is replaced by a Web Worker. Explicit braces clarify the original Russian roulette condition.
+- `public/render-worker.js`: loads the actual WASM module, renders passes, and transfers pixels to the page.
+- `app.js`: canvas, random palettes, settings, cancellation, original-scene reset, fullscreen, and PNG export. Changing a palette, resolution, or quality starts a fresh render. Stop preserves the current image.
+- `public/preview.png`: original-scene preview generated with this same WASM renderer at 800 × 600 and 256 samples per pixel, displayed while the first client-side pass loads.
+
+Randomization changes both the wall sphere colors and the visible mirror/glass sphere colors. Geometry, emission, and reflection/refraction materials stay as in the original scene. Presets render at 32, 128, or 512 samples per pixel. Rendering time depends on the device, resolution, and sample count.
+
+To regenerate the checked-in preview:
+
+```sh
+node scripts/render-preview.mjs
+```
+
+Upstream: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
