-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt in the browser

-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly and rendered onto a canvas in a dedicated module Web Worker. The home page is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`.

+## Build
+
+Requires Node.js, pnpm, and Emscripten (`em++` on PATH).

 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm build
 ```

-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+`pnpm build:wasm` regenerates the checked-in `public/wasm/smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm` assets. The regular build runs this step before Astro. Existing Wasm assets are included so the renderer can also be used without recompiling C++.
+
+The worker runs the original diffuse/specular/refractive radiance integrator with 2×2 subpixel antialiasing and Russian roulette. A buffer adapter replaces the original CLI/PPM output with RGBA rows. Six rows are transferred per update; rendering stays off the main thread. No pthreads, SharedArrayBuffer, or cross-origin isolation headers are required. Serve the built client assets over HTTP(S), with `.wasm` served as `application/wasm` for streaming compilation. No rendering API or server computation is used.
+
+The page starts a local render automatically. Randomize colors changes the two sphere and side-wall colors and immediately rerenders. Individual colors, resolution, samples per pixel, cancellation, reset, and PNG download are also available. The bundled preview is Kevin Beason’s original smallpt output (`result_25k.png` from the upstream distribution), resized to 800 × 600. It remains visible beneath incoming pixel rows until the fresh local render replaces it.
+
+Run `node scripts/verify-wasm.mjs` after compiling for a server-free runtime check of RGBA pixels, progressive row consistency, deterministic seeds, and sphere recoloring.
+
+## Source and license

-## Tech Stack
+- `native/smallpt-original.cpp`: unmodified upstream source.
+- `native/smallpt-core.h`: upstream integrator and scene with braces added to remove a dangling-else warning.
+- `native/renderer.cpp`: browser-facing buffer and color adapter.
+- `native/LICENSE.txt` and `public/wasm/LICENSE.txt`: Kevin Beason’s MIT license.
+- `public/wasm/render-worker.js`: Wasm initialization and transferable row buffers.
+- `src/pages/index.astro`: homepage.

-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+No browser verification or development/preview server was used during implementation.
