-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt — The render lab

-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason's [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The home page is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`; rendering runs entirely on the client in a module Web Worker, without rendering APIs or cross-origin isolation requirements.

+The page starts rendering automatically. **Randomize colors** changes the two walls and the mirror/glass sphere tints, then starts a fresh render. You can change resolution and sample count, stop or restart rendering, restore the original scene, and download a PNG.
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm build
+```
+
+The compiled `public/wasm/smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm` are included. Rebuilding the site does not require Emscripten. The home page and its `/studio.*`, `/wasm/`, `/favicon.svg`, and `/smallpt-preview.png` assets can be hosted statically from `dist/client/`. Other retained template routes use Astro's Node adapter.
+
+To recompile the renderer with `em++` on your PATH:
+
+```sh
+pnpm build:wasm
+pnpm check:wasm
+```
+
+To regenerate the initial PNG using the same WebAssembly renderer in Node:

 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm render:preview
 ```

-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+`native/smallpt-original.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source. `native/smallpt-web.cpp` adds an RGBA framebuffer, progressive 4-sample passes, deterministic per-row seeds, and a palette interface around the original integrator. It averages linear radiance across passes before gamma encoding. The renderer retains the original scene, ray/sphere intersections, diffuse/specular/refractive materials, and Russian roulette termination. OpenMP and PPM file output are replaced by one worker and canvas frames.

-## Tech Stack
+The checks execute the compiled WASM module in Node and verify visible opaque pixels, progressive rendering, changed output after tinting, and reproducible original-scene reset. No browser or server is needed for these checks.

-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+Original smallpt is copyright © 2006–2008 Kevin Beason and distributed under the MIT license. The complete notice is retained in `native/LICENSE.smallpt` and `public/wasm/LICENSE.txt`.
