+# The Daily Grind
+
+The page progressively enhances its static content with autonomous `<coffee-card>`
+elements. It needs no build step. Styles live in `index.html`; behavior lives in
+`coffee-card.js` and uses light DOM to preserve the existing content and theme.
+
+## Coffee card API
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Default | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `name` | string | `''` | Coffee heading |
+| `description` | string | `''` | Description text |
+| `href` | string | `''` | Details URL; only HTTP(S) URLs activate the link |
+| `price` | number or `null` | `null` | Optional USD price; zero is valid |
+| `featured` | boolean | `false` | Displays a seasonal favorite label |
+
+Properties reflect into attributes; attribute changes immediately update properties
+and connected content. String properties accept `null`/`undefined` to remove the
+attribute. `price = null` removes the price; invalid numeric assignments throw
+`RangeError`. Invalid or missing numeric attributes hide the price and read as
+`null`. Boolean attributes follow HTML presence semantics: `featured="false"` is
+still true; use `card.featured = false` or remove the attribute to disable it.
+
+```js
+const card = document.createElement('coffee-card');
+card.name = 'Maple Oat Latte';
+card.description = 'Oat milk and maple syrup.';
+card.href = '/menu/seasonal';
+card.price = 5.5;
+card.featured = true;
+document.querySelector('.grid').append(card);
+```
+
+Connection reuses existing content or creates it for programmatic instances.
+Disconnection removes the internal link listener, and reconnection restores it
+without duplicating content or listeners. Properties assigned before registration
+are recovered during upgrade. Attribute updates preserve existing content nodes.
+
+Activating the link emits a bubbling, composed, cancelable `coffee-card-select`
+event with `{ name, href, price, featured }` in `event.detail`. Calling
+`event.preventDefault()` cancels navigation. Native link navigation otherwise works
+normally.
