+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static page with autonomous `<coffee-card>` custom elements. Load
+`coffee-card.js` as a module once; registration upgrades existing cards automatically.
+Card styles live in shadow DOM and inherit the page's font, text color and CSS
+variables (`--primary` and `--accent` have standalone defaults).
+
+```html
+<script type="module" src="./coffee-card.js"></script>
+<coffee-card name="Maple Oat Latte" description="Oat milk and maple syrup."
+  href="/menu/seasonal" price="4.5" featured></coffee-card>
+```
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Default | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `name` | string | `""` | Heading and accessible link label. |
+| `description` | string | `""` | Description, rendered as plain text. |
+| `href` | string | `""` | Details URL; relative and HTTP(S) URLs supported. |
+| `price` | number or null | `null` | Optional USD price; finite and non-negative. |
+| `featured` | boolean | `false` | Highlights the card with the accent color. |
+| `disabled` | boolean | `false` | Disables details navigation and removes the link from tab order. |
+
+Properties reflect to attributes and attribute changes immediately update properties
+and rendering. Assigning `null` or `undefined` removes a string or numeric attribute.
+Invalid numeric attributes read as `null` and hide the price; invalid numeric property
+assignments throw `RangeError` and preserve the previous value. Numeric strings are
+accepted by the price setter.
+
+Boolean attributes use HTML presence semantics: `disabled="false"` is still true.
+Set `card.disabled = false` or remove the attribute to enable navigation. Boolean
+property assignments use JavaScript truthiness.
+
+The constructor creates the shadow DOM once. Connection restores properties set
+before registration, attaches the click listener and renders current attributes.
+Disconnection removes the listener; reconnecting reuses the same DOM and listener.
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm test` for automated DOM tests. No build step is required.
