diff --git a/EQUIPMENT.md b/EQUIPMENT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9f5ab13
--- /dev/null
+++ b/EQUIPMENT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Equipment connection setup
+
+The homepage makes direct, user-initiated GET requests from the browser. It does not proxy traffic, discover devices, start brewing, or keep a persistent session. Endpoint values are not stored or sent to the Daily Grind server.
+
+Defaults are illustrative: brewer `http://192.168.1.100/api/status`, desktop helper `http://127.0.0.1:45678/health`. Enter the actual complete status URL, including the port and path, in each card. The brewer accepts RFC 1918, link-local, IPv6 private addresses, and `.local` names. The helper accepts loopback addresses only.
+
+Serve the homepage over HTTPS (localhost is acceptable for local development). The browser independently handles `local-network` and `loopback-network` permission. Permission queries are feature-detected and unsupported queries fall back to an explicit click. Fetch uses the corresponding `targetAddressSpace` and displays actionable failures in browsers that cannot connect. No requests run on page load.
+
+Each endpoint must implement a safe GET health/status route returning a successful HTTP status (e.g. 200 or 204). No particular response body is required. Non-success HTTP responses fail the check. Configure `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` for the exact deployed Daily Grind origin. The request omits credentials; authenticated equipment needs an explicit pairing flow outside this panel. Redirects are rejected. Do not add deprecated Private Network Access preflight headers as a workaround for permission or CORS failures.
+
+The helper should bind to loopback only, validate permitted origins, and expose a read-only health route. The brewer must be reachable from the visitor’s network; isolated guest Wi-Fi cannot access private shop equipment without appropriate network configuration. Allow only the access intended by the shop.
+
+Run automated checks with `node --test equipment.test.mjs`. No server or browser is required.
