+# The Daily Grind account UI
+
+A static, responsive account page with passkey listing, renaming, deletion confirmation, last-key warning, empty/error states, and browser-provider sync support. The original storefront is preserved at `assets/original-storefront.html`.
+
+## Preview and integration
+
+This repository has no authentication service, database, or backend. By default the account screen is explicitly labeled **Preview account**. Sample credentials persist in local storage; preview mode never calls the real WebAuthn Signal API. No real sign-in access is revoked in preview mode.
+
+To connect the UI to an existing authenticated backend, add this to the HTML head:
+
+```html
+<meta name="daily-grind-account-api" content="/api/account">
+<meta name="csrf-token" content="SERVER_ISSUED_CSRF_TOKEN">
+```
+
+The API URL must be same-origin. The backend must supply the token dynamically if it requires CSRF tokens. Requests include session cookies and bypass the cache. Implement these routes:
+
+- `GET /api/account/credentials`: return the complete list for the authenticated customer, including `{ rpId, userId, profile: { displayName }, credentials: [...] }`.
+- `PUT /api/account/credential/:id`: validate and persist `{ name }` (trimmed, 1–60 characters). Respond with any successful 2xx status.
+- `DELETE /api/account/credential/:id`: revoke the credential on the server. Respond with any successful 2xx status.
+
+Every credential has `id`, `name`, raw epoch-millisecond `registeredAt` and optional `lastUsedAt`, plus optional `provider` (derived from registration AAGUID metadata) and `device` (`laptop`, `phone`, or `usb`). Missing provider/device metadata uses generic labels and icons. Do not return private or public credential key material. Credential IDs and `userId` must be unpadded Base64URL strings; `rpId` must be the actual server-configured registration RP ID.
+
+The server must require a signed-in session, enforce credential ownership on every route, validate nicknames, enforce same-origin/CSRF protections for writes, and return the full authoritative credential list (not a paginated subset). An expired session must return 401/403. The client never falls back to preview data when a live API fails. Passkey registration, account-profile editing, and authentication are outside this UI's scope; existing site routes remain integration points.
+
+## Authenticator synchronization
+
+In live mode the page calls `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials()` on load and after a successful deletion followed by a successful list refresh. It uses only server-provided RP/user/credential IDs and validates encoding. It also signals an empty list when the last key is deleted. Nickname changes are account labels and deliberately do not invoke `signalCurrentUserDetails()`.
+
+Synchronization is a passive enhancement: unsupported browsers and provider failures leave account operations usable and display manual password-manager cleanup guidance. A successful signal means the browser was notified; providers control whether saved entries are updated. Production needs HTTPS. Preview data is never sent to an authenticator.
+
+## Checks
+
+Run `node --test tests/passkeys.test.mjs` and `node --check assets/account.js`. No build step or runtime dependencies are needed. No development server or browser verification is required for these checks.
