@@ -15,3 +15,43 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Open `/devtools-times/account/settings` (also linked from **My account**). Signed-out
+readers see a labeled, interactive sample account; its edits stay in local storage
+and its sample credential IDs are never sent to an authenticator. Reset preview
+restores the sample keys. Signing in uses a server session and opens live settings.
+
+The local `/api/account/*` routes bridge to the existing account service. Set
+`ACCOUNT_API_URL` at build time to change the upstream API base; by default it is
+`https://us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api`.
+The upstream service must implement this contract (this repository does not contain
+that external service):
+
+- `POST /login`, accepting `{ username, password }`, returns a bearer `token` or
+  a session cookie. Credentials stay in the server session and are never returned
+  to the frontend. A service that returns only a success message must first add
+  authenticated sessions.
+- `GET /passkeys` returns the authenticated user's complete `PasskeyAccount`
+  snapshot described in `src/lib/passkeys.ts`. User IDs are WebAuthn user handles,
+  and credential IDs are base64url encoded. `rpId` is the actual relying party domain.
+- `PATCH /passkeys/:id`, accepting `{ displayName }`, renames an owned credential.
+- `DELETE /passkeys/:id` revokes an owned credential, so authentication must reject
+  it from then on. The upstream must authorize every operation for the session user.
+
+Mutation responses are followed by a fresh authoritative list request. The local
+bridge validates snapshots, rejects cross-origin writes, disables response caching,
+handles expired sessions and never fabricates a live passkey list when the upstream
+is unavailable. Configure durable, shared Astro session storage for multi-instance
+production deployments.
+
+After loading or changing a live list, browsers supporting WebAuthn's
+`signalAllAcceptedCredentials` receive its complete credential set, including an
+empty set after the last removal. Sync failures do not undo a saved server change;
+the UI offers retry and manual password-manager guidance. Passkey nicknames apply
+only to this site's list: WebAuthn does not expose a per-credential rename signal.
+See the [WebAuthn Signal API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/webauthn-signal-api).
+
+Automated checks: `node --experimental-strip-types --test tests/passkeys.test.ts`
+and `pnpm build`. Neither command starts a server.
