 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Reader accounts and passkeys
+
+Sign in and create an account at `/devtools-times/signin` and
+`/devtools-times/signup`. Account security is at `/devtools-times/account/settings`.
+The screens support passwordless registration, discoverable passkey sign-in,
+password fallback, passkey naming/removal, and explicit reauthentication.
+
+Authentication now uses this application's same-origin `/api/auth/*` endpoints.
+Accounts from the previous external sample API are not migrated; create a new
+local account to use this flow. Passwords are hashed with scrypt, passkeys are
+verified using SimpleWebAuthn, and session tokens are stored hashed with HttpOnly,
+SameSite cookies. WebAuthn challenges are single use and expire after five minutes.
+Passkey changes require recent verification; a passwordless account cannot remove
+its last passkey.
+
+Requires Node 22.13 or newer and HTTPS (localhost is permitted for development).
+Set `AUTH_ORIGIN` to the canonical public origin, without a trailing slash, when
+running behind a proxy, for example `https://news.example.com`. The RP ID is derived
+from this origin; changing domains requires registering new passkeys.
+
+Account data persists in `.data/accounts.sqlite` by default. Set
+`AUTH_DATABASE_PATH` to a path on a persistent writable volume for deployment.
+This SQLite store is intended for a single application instance. A multi-instance
+production deployment needs a shared database and shared rate limiting. The
+existing reading-list session remains separate from the reader account session.
+
+Build with `pnpm run build`. No browser or running server is required for the build.
