+# Privacy and third-party audit
+
+Reviewed 2026-11-19 using source inspection and automated static checks. No browser,
+live network audit, preview server, or production header verification was performed.
+
+## Current data inventory
+
+| Component | Data / purpose | Storage and recipients | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| HTML and CSS | Public coffee content | Public static hosting | Keep |
+| Hero photograph | Public image | Local `assets/coffee.jpg` | Removed visitor requests to Unsplash |
+| Fonts | System fonts | Already installed on visitor device | No font CDN |
+| Client scripts, analytics, ads, embeds, APIs | None | None | Block with CSP |
+| Forms, location, identifiers, cookies, Web Storage, IndexedDB, service workers | None | None | Do not introduce without review |
+| Hosting requests | IP address, URL and standard HTTP metadata needed to deliver pages | Hosting provider; log settings controlled by operator | Minimize logs before launch |
+
+The photograph was downloaded once during development from
+https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1350&q=80.
+No visitor contacts that origin. No third-party runtime dependencies are installed.
+`start` retains the existing development-only `pnpm dlx statikk` command; it is not
+part of the release and does not establish production security headers.
+
+The repository contains only the homepage and privacy page. Existing menu,
+account, ordering, rewards and contact links are placeholders for services outside
+this implementation. The former Logout link was removed because no session or
+logout endpoint exists. Do not imply that static navigation authenticates users,
+submits an order, or deletes server data.
+
+## Enforced browser boundaries
+
+- External CSS replaces inline styles. CSP allows only local styles and images;
+  scripts (including inline handlers), connections, workers, frames, plugins,
+  base URL overrides and form submission are blocked. No client script is needed.
+- `no-referrer` is set in both markup and response headers, before any resources
+  load. Powerful unused permissions are disabled in HTTP headers.
+- `_headers` supplies clickjacking protection, MIME sniffing protection, opener
+  and resource boundaries, and an initial five-minute HTTPS-only HSTS policy.
+  Increase HSTS after confirming HTTPS availability; subdomains and preload are
+  deliberately excluded because their HTTPS configuration is unknown.
+- CSP has no reporting endpoint or report samples: there is no report ingestion
+  service, and collecting violation payloads would create another data flow.
+  Do not configure a fictional endpoint. Any future reporting service must redact
+  URLs, queries, tokens and PII before storage and impose a short retention period.
+- No blanket `Clear-Site-Data` is sent during ordinary browsing. There is no local
+  personal data or session to clear in this implementation.
+
+## Deployment
+
+Run `npm run build` and publish **only `dist/`**. The build uses Node built-ins,
+audits the privacy boundaries and copies an explicit public-file allowlist.
+`netlify.toml` configures this build and publish directory; Netlify applies the
+included `_headers` file to all static responses. Cloudflare Pages can also use
+that file when publishing `dist/` without Functions. Other hosts must translate
+the same rules into their HTTP/CDN configuration; merely serving `_headers` as a
+file does not apply them.
+
+The markup CSP is a fallback. `frame-ancestors`, Permissions-Policy and the other
+HTTP-only protections require actual response headers. Do not claim those are
+active on an arbitrary static server. Ensure production serves HTTPS and the
+correct HTML, CSS and JPEG MIME types. Disable injected analytics, tag managers,
+third-party error reporting and automatic form collection in the hosting account.
+
+Before launch, the operator must configure hosting access/security log retention
+and access controls, document the actual duration in the public privacy notice,
+and make the Contact Us channel operational. Do not log request bodies,
+authorization headers, cookies or full URL queries. Omit or truncate IP addresses
+where possible; restrict log access and automatically expire retained logs.
+
+## Changes that require another review
+
+Run `npm run check:privacy` for every release. It is a source regression guard,
+not a full HTML parser or proof of deployed behavior. The checks reject new active
+content, external resource URLs and policy drift. Review new HTML files and changes
+to the checks themselves. Review dependencies and hosting integrations every
+quarter and whenever vendors change; record origins, data fields, purpose,
+retention, deletion support, subprocessors and approval in the inventory above.
+Audit a sanitized production HAR when live verification is separately authorized;
+never commit HARs containing credentials or personal data.
+
+For future features:
+
+- Collect only fields needed for the immediate task, explain purpose beside the
+  input, make optional fields optional and permit guest checkout. Do not reuse
+  order data for marketing without a separate, optional opt-in.
+- Do not place personal information or credentials in URLs, browser storage or
+  client logs. Use HTTPS, server validation, authorization and rate limits. Render
+  text with `textContent`; never interpolate untrusted HTML or execute strings.
+- Keep sessions server-side with `__Host-` cookies using `Secure`, `HttpOnly`,
+  `SameSite=Lax`, `Path=/` and no Domain. Protect state changes with CSRF defenses.
+  Logout must be a protected server-side action that invalidates the session,
+  expires its cookie, returns `Cache-Control: no-store`, and sends
+  `Clear-Site-Data: "cookies", "storage", "cache"`. Authenticated pages also need
+  `Cache-Control: no-store`. Client storage clearing cannot invalidate a session.
+- Define retention/deletion jobs and verified access, correction, export and
+  deletion flows when introducing server-held data. Do not offer simulated
+  account deletion in a static page.
+- Prefer self-hosted assets and plain sharing links over SDKs. If an embed becomes
+  necessary, use a local facade and connect only after explicit user action;
+  disclose the recipient and purpose first. Audit even thumbnail and font hosts.
+  Pin immutable third-party scripts/styles, verify build-time SRI and use anonymous
+  CORS and `no-referrer`. Change the CSP only for the reviewed capability.
+
+References: [Netlify custom headers](https://docs.netlify.com/manage/routing/headers/)
+and [MDN frame-ancestors limitations](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/frame-ancestors).
