+# Privacy engineering and third-party audit
+
+Reviewed November 19, 2026. Scope: the static pages, CSS, image, build tooling,
+and deployment header configuration in this repository. No account, order,
+payment, or other backend implementation is present.
+
+## Data minimization
+
+The published site contains no browser JavaScript, forms, analytics, cookies,
+browser storage, tracking pixels, fingerprinting, or third-party embeds. System
+fonts and local assets avoid third-party requests. No consent state or visitor
+identifier is created. The privacy notice is available at `/privacy-policy/`.
+The unimplemented GET logout link was removed; future logout must use a
+CSRF-protected state-changing request.
+
+## Third-party inventory
+
+| Component | Browser exposure | Decision |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Unsplash hero photo | Previously contacted images.unsplash.com on each page load | Downloaded the existing stock image into assets/coffee.jpg; no runtime request remains |
+| Fonts | System fonts only | No external font provider |
+| Analytics, ads, embeds, runtime SDKs | None found | Keep absent by default |
+| Hosting provider | Receives IP address, URL, and connection metadata | Operator must review access logs, retention, region, subprocessors, and access controls before deployment |
+| Development server command | pnpm dlx statikk downloads tooling when explicitly run | Not a public runtime dependency; not run for this change |
+| Build and security checks | Node built-ins only | No added packages or network calls |
+
+Image source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085
+The original image remains unchanged; only its delivery location changed.
+
+Review additions before shipping: purpose, necessity, fields collected, vendor
+recipients, retention/deletion, and browser network/storage behavior. Optional
+tracking must remain off until an appropriate consent mechanism is implemented.
+Do not add preconnect, DNS prefetch, remote fonts, or link tracking parameters.
+
+## Deployment and secure handling
+
+Run `npm run build` and publish **dist/**. The `_headers` file uses the Netlify /
+Cloudflare Pages static header format. On other hosts, translate these rules
+into the host's HTTP response configuration. The existing `start` command is
+only a file server and is not configured to enforce `_headers`. HTML meta CSP
+and referrer policy provide a partial fallback; framing restrictions, HSTS,
+Permissions-Policy, and other response headers require hosting support.
+Cloudflare worker/function responses need their own header configuration.
+
+Serve exclusively over HTTPS and redirect HTTP at the edge. HSTS is intentionally
+limited to the current host, without preload or includeSubDomains, because this
+repository does not establish the security of other subdomains. Check the live
+HTTP response headers after deployment; repository tests cannot establish what
+a host actually sends. No deployment or live browser verification was performed.
+
+The CSP blocks scripts, connections, forms, plugins, workers, and framing, and
+allows local styles and images. Referrers are suppressed; sensitive browser
+capabilities are disabled. Pages are marked no-store. This does not delete
+existing browser caches or control hosting logs. Avoid personal information in
+URLs and avoid logging cookies, authorization headers, bodies, or full query
+strings. Configure minimum necessary log retention and restrict operator access.
+No telemetry/reporting endpoint is configured, since reports can disclose URLs.
+
+Future account/payment services require a new review and scoped policy changes.
+Validate inputs on the server, encode output, use HTTPS, CSRF protection,
+Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite session cookies, server-side authorization, limited
+retention, and working deletion mechanisms. Never store credentials, tokens,
+payment data, or personal records in localStorage, source files, or public assets.
+Collect only fields required for the disclosed purpose. Publish the actual
+service providers, retention periods, and privacy contact before collection.
+
+## Automated checks
+
+`npm test` audits all source HTML/CSS, rejects external URLs, scripts, collection
+controls, and unsafe inline content, and checks CSP parity and response headers.
+`npm run build` runs that audit before copying an explicit set of public files.
+These checks enforce this site's current conservative baseline; they are not a
+substitute for a hosting configuration audit or a backend security assessment.
