+The homepage includes in-page sign-in. This repository serves static files only;
+it does not include a customer database or an authentication service. Deploy the
+following same-origin endpoints before enabling real customer authentication:
+
+| Endpoint | Contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| `GET /api/login/session` | Return JSON `{ "authenticated": true }` only for a valid server session; otherwise return `false` for that property. |
+| `POST /api/login/options` | Accept `{}` and return discoverable WebAuthn request options as JSON, including a Base64URL challenge, the configured `rpId`, and an empty or omitted `allowCredentials`. Bind the challenge and expected user verification policy to the server session. |
+| `POST /api/login/verify` | Accept the assertion serialized by `PublicKeyCredential.toJSON()`. Verify the challenge, origin, RP ID, signature, and user verification policy using a maintained WebAuthn server library. Resolve the customer from the verified credential. Return 404 specifically for an unknown credential ID. |
+| `POST /api/login/password` | Accept JSON `{ "username": "…", "password": "…" }`, validate the password against the customer database, and reject invalid credentials. |
+
+Both verification endpoints must establish a server session using a Secure,
+HttpOnly, SameSite cookie and return JSON `{ "authenticated": true }` only after
+successful verification. Reject failed verification with a non-success status.
+Protect these endpoints against cross-origin requests and login abuse, and serve
+authentication responses with `Cache-Control: no-store`. Production requires HTTPS.
+Do not log submitted passwords or assertions. The client never treats the browser's
+credential selection as proof of authentication.
+
+The browser offers passive passkey autofill while customers browse. Unmodified
+Rewards, My Account, Order Now, and Sign in clicks request the immediate browser
+chooser only when `immediateGet` is supported and server options are ready. Other
+browsers and cancellations retain the inline form. The explicit passkey button
+uses the standard prompt, so cross-device passkeys remain available. Successful
+verification resumes the selected destination; Keep browsing clears it.
+
+`vendor/webauthn-polyfills-0.1.7.mjs` is the pinned browser bundle of
+`webauthn-polyfills` 0.1.7, sourced from
+`https://esm.sh/webauthn-polyfills@0.1.7/es2022/webauthn-polyfills.bundle.mjs`.
+It is served locally so sign-in does not depend on a third-party CDN at runtime.
