+# Daily Grind
+
+Run `npm start` to serve the homepage and newsletter API with Node.js 20+.
+`PORT` defaults to 11222. No dependencies or build step are needed.
+
+Signups are saved to `data/newsletter.jsonl` with restricted file permissions.
+Set `DATA_DIR` to a persistent, private directory in production and back it up.
+Only the homepage, CSS, and JavaScript are publicly served; signup data is never
+available through the static routes. This collects signups; it does not send
+newsletters or verification emails.
+
+The server sends an enforced Content-Security-Policy on every response. Scripts,
+styles, API connections, and form submissions are restricted to the same origin.
+Images may also load from `https://images.unsplash.com`. Inline scripts, inline
+styles, framing, plugins, and workers are blocked. CSP reduces injection risk;
+allowed origins still need to be trusted. Serve through HTTPS in production.
+
+`npm test` checks the request handler directly with simulated requests; it does
+not open a listening server or import the server entrypoint.
