+# SMS sign-in
+
+The static homepage runs in an explicitly labeled preview mode. Request a code
+with a valid phone number, then enter `123456`. This never sends an SMS, creates
+an authenticated session, or stores the phone number. The code expires after
+five minutes; resend is available after 30 seconds.
+
+To enable real sign-in, define this configuration before `auth.js` loads:
+
+```html
+<script>window.DAILY_GRIND_AUTH = { apiBase: '/api/auth' };</script>
+```
+
+Provide two same-origin JSON endpoints:
+
+- `POST /api/auth/send` receives `{ phone, purpose }` where phone is E.164 and
+  purpose is `rewards` or `order`. Send a random six-digit code and return
+  `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-issued-id" }`.
+- `POST /api/auth/verify` receives `{ challengeId, code, purpose }`. Validate the
+  challenge on the server, establish a secure HttpOnly session, and return
+  `{ "verified": true }`. Success links to `/rewards` or `/order`; those existing
+  destinations must enforce authentication independently.
+- Errors use non-2xx responses and `{ "error": "INVALID_CODE" }`,
+  `EXPIRED_CODE`, or `RATE_LIMITED`. Other errors get a generic retry message.
+
+The server must enforce five-minute expiry, single use, send/attempt rate limits,
+phone validation, origin/CSRF checks, and binding the challenge to its phone and
+session. Client timers are only interface feedback. Never expose provider secrets
+or the real code to client JavaScript. Both destinations share the same sign-in;
+users can switch their intended destination while entering the code.
+
+Send an origin-bound SMS whose final line contains the actual production host:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind sign-in code is 654321. It expires in 5 minutes.
+
+@your-domain.example #654321
+```
+
+Use HTTPS. Supported browsers can extract the code with WebOTP after permission;
+platform autofill uses `autocomplete="one-time-code"`. Everyone can type or paste
+into the same labeled numeric input. The user explicitly confirms verification.
+WebOTP requests stop on submission, resend, number changes, navigation, or timeout.
+Implementation follows the [Chrome WebOTP guidance](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp).
+
+Run static behavior checks with `node --test auth.test.cjs`. No build dependencies
+or server are required.
