index 4479b53..6469e54 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,35 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Set the server runtime variables listed in [.env.example](.env.example):
+`TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, `TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID`, and
+`SMS_ORIGIN`. The Messaging Service needs an SMS-capable sender. Configure its
+allowed destinations and spending controls before enabling public sign-ups.
+Use the exact public origin for `SMS_ORIGIN`, without a path or trailing slash.
+The standalone server reads these from its process environment; keep credentials
+out of client variables and source control.
+
+The form collects account details and an international phone number, then sends
+a six-digit SMS code. The last SMS line is `@your-domain #123456` so WebOTP and
+device SMS autofill can match the site. WebOTP requires HTTPS (localhost is
+supported for development); manual typing and pasting always remain available.
+The server rejects invalid, expired, or exhausted challenges before forwarding
+registration, and never returns the code to the browser. Codes expire after ten
+minutes and allow five attempts. Resends wait sixty seconds, with hourly phone
+and IP limits. SMS/provider errors do not expose credentials or provider details.
+
+Challenges and rate limits currently live in one Node process, with an opaque
+challenge ID in the Astro session. A restart requires requesting another code.
+Before running multiple replicas, replace the maps in `src/lib/server/signup.ts`
+with a shared store supporting atomic consumption and rate limits, and configure
+shared Astro sessions. This application gates its own registration route; the
+existing external registration service must independently enforce verification
+if direct registration against that service also needs to be restricted. It
+receives the verified `phoneNumber`, but persistence of that field depends on its
+API contract.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for mocked SMS/registration tests and `pnpm run build` for the
+production build. Tests never send actual texts or start a server.
