+
+## Sign-up SMS verification
+
+The sign-up form uses the same-origin `POST /devtools-times/api/signup` endpoint.
+Its `send` action requests an SMS from Twilio Verify; its `register` action checks
+that code with Twilio before forwarding the username, password, and normalized
+`phoneNumber` to the existing registration service. Codes and credentials are not
+stored in browser storage or logged. A failed registration after code approval
+requires a new code because approved Twilio codes cannot be reused.
+
+Configure the server runtime with the variables in `.env.example` (for a deployed
+Node server, inject environment variables through your hosting platform).
+Create a Twilio Verify service with **6-digit** codes, configure permitted SMS
+destinations and Verify rate limits/Fraud Guard, and supply its service SID,
+account SID, and auth token. Missing configuration returns a service-unavailable
+message and never claims that a text was sent. Trial accounts can only send to
+verified recipients. The external registration service remains independently
+accessible: enforcing phone verification for every possible registration client
+also requires enforcement in that service, whose source is outside this repo.
+
+For automatic SMS extraction, serve the site over HTTPS and configure an approved
+[Twilio domain-bound SMS template](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/verification-templates),
+either as the service default or via `TWILIO_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_SID`. The SMS must end
+with the actual sign-up page's hostname and the code, for example:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is: 123456
+
+@your-hostname.example #123456
+```
+
+Use a hostname only (no protocol, path, or port). WebOTP reads a message with user
+consent in supported browsers; `autocomplete="one-time-code"` provides OS autofill
+hints elsewhere. Manual typing and pasting work in all browsers. See the
+[WebOTP documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp).
+
+Run the mocked verification tests with `node --test tests/signup.test.mjs` and
+compile the app with `pnpm build`. Tests do not send SMS or create accounts.
