+# The Daily Grind
+
+A responsive coffee homepage with rewards registration using the browser Email Verification API (EVP). No OTP or magic link is sent. Unsupported, missing, invalid, and expired proofs never create a verified account.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Requires Node 24+ and pnpm. Install dependencies with `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and configure:
+
+- `APP_ORIGIN`: the exact public HTTPS origin. Required in production. Register this origin for the [Chrome Email Verification origin trial](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/email-verification/verifier).
+- `EVP_ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN`: a valid trial token for that origin. Older trial tokens expired November 17, 2026; use a renewed Chrome 160 extension token. The server sends it as an `Origin-Trial` response header.
+- `DATABASE_PATH`: a writable SQLite path on persistent storage. Default `data/rewards.sqlite`. Use a single Node instance; keep the database and its WAL files together and back them up.
+- `PORT`: defaults to 11222. TLS should terminate at your reverse proxy. `APP_ORIGIN` sets the expected origin and secure-cookie behavior; proxy forwarded headers are deliberately not trusted.
+
+`pnpm build` checks JavaScript syntax and runs offline cryptographic/storage checks without starting or importing the server, then packages server and assets in `dist/`. `pnpm start` is the production entry command when you are ready to run it. The application has not been started as part of this change.
+
+## Registration
+
+The server renders an email field (`autocomplete="email"`) and a hidden `autocomplete="email-verification-token"` field with a random session nonce. Native form submission lets the browser populate the signed token. A first-party HttpOnly, SameSite cookie binds the nonce to the form session.
+
+`POST /api/rewards/signup` accepts URL-encoded form data or JSON with `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`, `token`, `csrf` (the issued nonce), `terms: "yes"`, and optional `marketing: "yes"`. The `Origin` header must exactly match `APP_ORIGIN`. GET the homepage with the same cookie jar first to obtain the challenge. Form submissions redirect back with a server-held flash message; JSON requests receive structured errors or 201 on success. The nonce is consumed before provider validation. Reload the homepage for a new challenge after every JSON attempt.
+
+Server verification uses `@sd-jwt/core` and `jose` to check the issuer signature, key-binding signature, digest, audience, nonce, email, verified claim, and freshness. DNS delegation must authorize the issuer. Network access is pinned to the Google discovery and JWKS endpoints; additional providers require an explicit trust-list change. HTTP redirects and arbitrary token-supplied destinations are rejected. This release supports Gmail's participating issuer. Both browser support and a signed-in provider session are needed.
+
+Verified accounts are stored in SQLite with 50 welcome points, marketing consent, and terms version. Unique email constraints prevent duplicate welcome bonuses. The server limits signup attempts by socket IP (15 per 10 minutes); behind a proxy this can be shared across visitors, so configure a trusted edge limiter for larger deployments. Tokens are never persisted or logged. Verification establishes email ownership for registration; no returning-user authentication or purchase/points integration is included.
+
+Browser/provider failures display a retry message and preserve the entered names and email. There is deliberately no email fallback. Terms and privacy details open in accessible dialogs.
+
+## Validation
+
+Offline build checks exercise signed success proofs, missing proofs, email/audience/nonce mismatches, unverified claims, expiry and freshness, invalid signatures, digest tampering, DNS delegation, untrusted network destinations, replay prevention, duplicate membership, welcome points, and rate limits. No browser verification or server startup is required.
+
+Stock imagery: Unsplash. Fonts: Google Fonts (DM Sans and Playfair Display).
