+# Daily Grind components
+
+Load `daily-grind.js` once using a module script. It registers four autonomous custom elements with open shadow roots, cloned templates, native HTML semantics, and encapsulated styles. No dependencies or build step are required.
+
+| Element | Named slots | Default slot |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `coffee-card` | `heading` (heading element), `action` (link) | Description |
+| `grind-hero` | `heading` (page heading), `action` (link) | Introductory content |
+| `grind-navigation` | `brand` (home link) | Navigation links |
+| `grind-footer` | `link` (footer links) | Copyright or other content |
+
+```html
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="heading">House Blend</h3>
+  <p>Freshly roasted every morning.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/house-blend"
+     aria-label="View details for House Blend">View Details</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+Keep headings in document order, use the appropriate heading level for the surrounding page, and give repeated link text a descriptive accessible name. Content and native links remain readable and usable if JavaScript is unavailable. Slots accept live DOM content without interpolating it into HTML strings.
+
+The navigation uses a native button below 700px. Enter/Space toggle the links; Escape closes them and returns focus to the button. Collapsed links leave the tab order. Resizing preserves visibility of focused links, and disconnecting the component removes its listeners; reconnecting initializes them again. Each instance keeps its button and controlled panel in the same shadow root, so their ARIA relationship stays local.
+
+Components inherit font, line height, and text color. Theme them with `--primary`, `--secondary`, `--accent`, `--text`, and `--focus-ring`; cards also accept `--card-background`, and the hero accepts `--hero-image` (a CSS `url(...)`). The card, hero, and footer expose matching `part` names for intentional style overrides. Page layout, section spacing, and sticky positioning stay in the page stylesheet.
+
+The module only uses browser APIs and must be loaded client-side. It does not import or start a server.
