+Load `daily-grind.js` once with a module script to register three native Web Components. No runtime dependencies or build step are required.
+
+- `grind-navigation`: place navigation links in its default slot. The optional `brand` slot replaces the brand text. Below 701px, a native button controls the links; Escape closes the menu and returns focus to the button. Event listeners are removed on disconnection.
+- `coffee-hero`: place a heading, description, and call-to-action link in its default slot. Use the appropriate heading level for the page.
+- `coffee-card`: supply a heading in `slot="title"`, descriptive content in `slot="description"`, and a link in `slot="action"`. Give repeated link text a descriptive accessible name that includes its visible text.
+
+Content stays in HTML and links remain available without JavaScript. Each component owns its layout and interaction styles in an independent shadow root. Global typography and CSS custom properties inherit into the components: `--primary`, `--accent`, and `--hero-image` (a CSS `url(...)` value). Avoid global selectors that reset slotted headings and links, since light DOM rules take precedence over shadow slot styles.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for DOM-based checks of slots, semantic content, mobile navigation, focus restoration, viewport changes, and lifecycle cleanup. These checks do not launch a browser or server.
