 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser tools (WebMCP)
+
+In browsers with WebMCP enabled, the header forms expose `open_search` and
+`get_reading_list` on every page. Opening search exposes `search_articles`
+(`query`); opening the reading list exposes `toggle_reading_list` (`slug`).
+The toggle saves an absent article or removes a saved article. Form submissions
+return results through the native agent SubmitEvent and also update the visible
+UI. Ordinary mouse and keyboard submissions use the same handlers.
+
+The shared layout registers four client-side article utilities once per document:
+`get_plant_stats`, `get_tide_levels`, `brew_coffee`, and
+`get_article_popularity` (requires an article `id`, such as `super-bowl-lx`).
+They use the configured base URL and report response data, HTTP status, and
+redirects. The existing article examples' intentional HTTP failures remain intact.
+Registration uses `document.modelContext`, with a fallback for older
+`navigator.modelContext` implementations. Browsers without this API retain the
+normal UI. Tools persist across Astro client navigation without being registered
+again.
+
+See Chrome's [declarative form API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api)
+and [imperative tool API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api).
+
+Run the focused checks with Node.js 24 or later:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/browser-tools.test.ts
+pnpm run build
+```
